+          <h2 data-otp-label="Four kinds of friction" style="font-size:1.9rem;margin:8px 0 12px;">Four kinds of Accessibility Friction, one practice</h2>
           <p style="color:var(--ink);max-width:46rem;">When a form, a doorway, a hiring process, or the tool stack itself was not built for them, people have to push harder, wait longer, and find a way around it. That daily drag is Accessibility Friction, and it builds in four places.</p>
           <details class="more-text"><summary>See the four places as a chart</summary><div class="more-body"><figure class="diagram"><svg viewBox="0 0 880 372" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Four kinds of Accessibility Friction, one practice"><text x="440" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Libre Franklin, sans-serif" font-size="19" font-weight="700" fill="#102A43">Four kinds of Accessibility Friction, one practice</text><text x="24" y="84" font-family="Libre Franklin, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#102A43">Digital Friction</text><rect x="24" y="96" width="832" height="24" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="24" y="96" width="640" height="24" rx="8" fill="#2563EB"/><text x="24" y="152" font-family="Libre Franklin, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#102A43">Physical Friction</text><rect x="24" y="164" width="832" height="24" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="24" y="164" width="540" height="24" rx="8" fill="#0F766E"/><text x="24" y="220" font-family="Libre Franklin, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#102A43">Communications and</text><text x="24" y="242" font-family="Libre Franklin, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#102A43">Workplace Friction</text><rect x="24" y="254" width="832" height="24" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="24" y="254" width="460" height="24" rx="8" fill="#9A3412"/><text x="24" y="310" font-family="Libre Franklin, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#102A43">Technology Friction</text><rect x="24" y="322" width="832" height="24" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="24" y="322" width="370" height="24" rx="8" fill="#102A43"/></svg><figcaption>Infographic: the four kinds of friction this practice is built to close. Diagram bars are illustrative of scope, not measured figures.</figcaption></figure></div></details>
           <ul class="friction-index friction-grid"><li><span class="tag">Friction 1</span><div><h3>Digital Friction</h3><p class="small">Websites, forms, portals, PDFs, and application processes. This is the friction the two web deadlines above are asking you to remove.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-digital">Read the full Digital Friction card</a></p></div></li><li><span class="tag">Friction 2</span><div><h3>Physical Friction</h3><p class="small">Buildings, routes, parking, counters, signage, restrooms, meeting rooms, event spaces, and voting places. The barrier a visitor meets first is usually at arrival.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-physical">Read the full Physical Friction card</a></p></div></li><li><span class="tag">Friction 3</span><div><h3>Communications and Workplace Friction</h3><p class="small">The Title I part: hiring, onboarding, employee rights and resources, the accommodation process, etiquette, support, and awareness inside the workplace.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-comms">Read the full Communications and Workplace Friction card</a></p></div></li><li><span class="tag">Friction 4</span><div><h3>Technology Friction</h3><p class="small">The wrong software, or too much of it: too many overlapping tools, none of them quite right, costing time every day.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-technology">Read the full Technology Friction card</a></p></div></li></ul><details class="more-text"><summary>See how it compounds, and the prevention</summary><div class="more-body"><p>Left standing, it does not stay in those four places. It compounds into three more: Legal Friction, Time Friction, and Bottom-line Friction.</p><ul class="friction-index"><li><span class="tag">Friction 5</span><div><h3>Legal Friction</h3><p class="small">What ADA non-compliance becomes over time: complaints, investigations, and lawsuits, including class actions, aimed at barriers that were visible, reported, or documented and still left standing.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-legal">Read the full Legal Friction card</a></p></div></li><li><span class="tag">Friction 6</span><div><h3>Time Friction</h3><p class="small">The time Legal Friction pulls out of the week: leadership time, legal time, and staff time spent responding to a problem instead of doing the planned work that would have prevented it.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-time">Read the full Time Friction card</a></p></div></li><li><span class="tag">Friction 7</span><div><h3>Bottom-line Friction</h3><p class="small">What executives see in the numbers: penalties, legal and settlement costs, remediation done in a rush at a premium, and the quieter loss of customers, residents, and employees who hit a barrier and never come back.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-bottomline">Read the full Bottom-line Friction card</a></p></div></li><li><span class="tag warm">The prevention</span><div><h3>The work that stops the compounding</h3><p class="small">Training that stops new friction being built, audits and assessments that name what is standing, remediation that removes it, and transition planning that sequences the rest with owners and dates.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><a href="#debt" class="quiet-link" data-go="debt" data-jump="friction-prevention">Read the full prevention card</a></p></div></li></ul><p style="max-width:46rem;margin-top:18px;">People reveal this friction every day. When the paved route does not go where people need to go, they carve a desire path across the grass. People vote with their actions. Frame it correctly: they are revealing friction in the system, not misbehaving. This practice reads those signals, measures the friction, and puts the fixes in an order your team can finish.</p></div></details><div class="btnrow"><a href="#debt" class="btn ghost" data-go="debt">Read the full Friction cards in Reference</a></div>
